# CamillaDSP's log (camilladsp.service passes `-o /opt/vibesbox-src/state/camilladsp.log`).
#
# ⚠ WHY THIS EXISTS: found 2026-09-07 at 10 GB — ~35 % of the 29 GB card — having grown since
# the Sep 6 boot, i.e. on the order of GB/day. Nothing had ever read it, and nothing bounded it.
#
# ⛔ THE SIZE IS A SYMPTOM, NOT THE FAULT. The volume is repeated
#   `WARN [camillalib::pipewire_backend::device] Capture: processing pipeline full, dropping frame`
# — CamillaDSP discarding capture frames, mid-chain, continuously. Rotating it bounds the disk
# and DOES NOT fix that. Do not treat this file as having closed the issue.
#
# `copytruncate` is mandatory: camilladsp holds the fd from `-o` open for the life of the
# process and does not reopen on signal, so a plain rename leaves it writing to an unlinked
# inode and the disk never comes back.
#
# ⚠ `copytruncate` COPIES the live file, so the rotation threshold is also the copy cost on an
# SD card. 20M keeps each copy cheap; the trade is that at a GB/day drop rate the daily
# logrotate timer is far too slow, hence the hourly override installed alongside this.
/opt/vibesbox-src/state/camilladsp.log {
    size 20M
    rotate 3
    compress
    delaycompress
    copytruncate
    missingok
    notifempty
    su root root
}
